brick:Disconnect_Switch rdfs:label "Disconnect Switch"@en ,
                                   "Disconnect Switch" ;
                        skos:definition "A disconnect switch performs the task of manually cutting or reconnecting power from an electrical supply by creating or closing an air insulation gap between two conduction points. Also known as an 'Isolation Switch'."@en ,
                                        "Building power is most commonly provided by utility company through a master disconnect switch (sometimes called a service disconnect) in the main electrical room of a building. The Utility Company provided master disconnect switch often owns or restricts access to this switch. There can also be other cases where a disconnect is placed into an electrical system to allow service cut-off to a portion of the building."@en ;
